      "id": 1,
      "text": "Woodstock was renamed from Centerville in 1845 after Joel Johnson’s hometown Woodstock, Vermont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodstock%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Woodstock was founded as Centerville in 1844 and became the county seat of McHenry County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://woodstockil.gov/482/Woodstock-History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic downtown Square anchors the Woodstock Opera House and the Old McHenry County Courthouse, both on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodstock%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Chicago and Northwestern railroad arrived in the mid‑1800s, opening Chicago markets for local farmers and attracting the Borden Dairy plant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
